  "answer": "This is a known issue. The screens going black is a Windows desktop composition (DWM) reset, and PowerToys then throws the 'Desktop composition is disabled' (0x80263001) exception and shows its 'Something went wrong' window. All the past tickets were closed as duplicates of PowerToys#31226, so that is the ticket to follow for updates. The maintainers' advice in those tickets was to update PowerToys to the latest version, since 0.86.0 is old. You can also subscribe to or add a thumbs-up on #31226. The past tickets don't give any other workaround."
